  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR fixes two defects in the Siemens 840D post (`assets/posts/sinumerik.cps`).\n\n**#4143: the D word of the tool call.** The post wrote `T<n> D<n> M6`, so tool 12 got `D12`. D selects an offset data block of the active tool. With \"D number = cutting edge number\", each tool has D1 to D12 for its cutting edges. Thus `D12` selects an edge that tool 12 does not have. The result is an alarm, or an empty edge with no length.\n- The tool call now writes `T<n> D1 M6`.\n- A new optional machine-file fact, `tooling.d_number`, selects the rule: `first-edge` (the default, D1) or `tool-number` (D equal to T, for a control set to free D numbers).\n- The machine file reader refuses any other value by name (`machine file: tooling.d_number: ...`). The post reads the fact as `machine.dNumber`. The machine sheet shows it in the General group.\n- The wear-compensation note names the same D word.\n\n**#4144: the G53 retracts.** Each G53 Z retract is now `G0 G53 Z<safe> D0`. This includes the setup-change lift, the home ask and the program end.\n- The program end wrote `G53 Z..` with no `G0`. G53 is not a motion word. After a `G1` the move used the feed rate, and after `G2`/`G3` the control gives an alarm.\n- G53 does not deselect the tool length. With the length active, the tool tip went to the safe Z, and the spindle went the tool length higher. `D0` deselects the tool offset in the same block.\n- A later section that keeps the same tool (no tool change) writes `D1` (or the stated D rule) before its first move. Its first traverse states its height again.\n\nCode: `crates/post/src/machine/{installation,def,parse,mod}.rs` and `crates/post/src/post/machine_installation.rs` (the fact, its mirror and the script property), `crates/app/src/machine/sheet.rs` (one sheet row), `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` (the key), `docs/decisions/4143-sinumerik-d-and-g53.md`.\n\n## Manual references\n\nSINUMERIK 840D sl Programming Manual Fundamentals, 12/2018 (A5E40869423B AB):\n- Section 6.6 \"Tool offset call (D)\", pp. 82-83: D activates an offset data block of the active tool. \"When D0 is programmed, offsets for the tool have no effect.\" \"Type of D programming\" is set by machine data: \"D number = cutting edge number\" (D1 to D12 for each tool) or \"free selection of D numbers\". The length applies with the first traverse of the length axis.\n- Section 9.1, p. 151, and section 13.10, p. 358: G53 suppresses the settable and programmable frames non-modally. G153 and SUPA suppress more frames and offsets. None of them deselects the tool offset, and none is a motion word.\n- Section 4.4, pp. 54-55: the program example retracts with `N5 G0 G53 X280 Z380 D0` and `N130 G0 G53 X280 Z380 D0 M5`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Tool 12, no machine: `N20 T12 D1 M6` (was `T12 D12 M6`).\n- Machine file with `\"tooling\": {\"d_number\": \"tool-number\"}`: `T12 D12 M6`.\n- Program end on the default VMC: `G0 G53 Z0 D0`, then `M2` (was `G53 Z0`).\n- Home ask, then a section with the same tool: `G0 G53 Z0 D0`, `G0 G53 X0 Y0`, the preamble, `D1`, `S2000 M3`, `G0 Z5`, then the first XY move.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/sinumerik_safe_retract.rs` (joins the existing 840D retract suite; no new test binary):\n- `every_g53_retract_is_a_rapid_that_cancels_the_tool_offset` (red on main)\n- `a_section_after_a_retract_with_the_same_tool_selects_the_d_again` (red on main)\n- `the_tool_call_selects_the_first_cutting_edge_by_default` (red on main)\n- `a_machine_stating_tool_number_d_writes_d_equal_to_t` (the D = T output is what main wrote; the test pins the machine-file rule and the refusal of an unknown value)\n- The three existing tests now expect `G0 G53 Z.. D0`.\n\n`crates/app/tests/program_comments.rs`: the Sinumerik tool line is now `T3 D1 M6`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nThe goldens were written again with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`. Each changed line is one of these three kinds. No other line changed.\n1. `G53 Z0` changed to `G0 G53 Z0 D0` (30 program ends, #4144). The explain golden reads `G0 G53 Z0 D0 ; RAPID MOVE, MACHINE COORDINATES FOR THIS BLOCK`.\n2. `T<n> D<n> M6` changed to `T<n> D1 M6` for tools 2, 3, 4, 5 and 7 (#4143). Tool 1 lines did not change (D1 already).\n3. The explain golden: `T3 D3 M6 ; TOOL 3, TOOL CHANGE` changed to `T3 D1 M6 ; TOOL 3, TOOL CHANGE`.\n\nFiles:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinumerik/*.nc` (17 files, conformance, control_comp, wear_comp, probe_op, solid_law_goldens)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/sinumerik/{contour_plate_with_hole,drill_peck}.nc` (program_units)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_sinumerik.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sinumerik/*.nc` (7 files, script_sinumerik)\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/{bore,ream,explain}/sinumerik.nc`, `crates/post/tests/golden/wcs_flip/sinumerik_x.nc`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real 840D control. The behaviour comes only from the cited manual pages.\n- The `tool-number` rule was not checked against a control that is set to free D numbers.\n\n## Gate\n\nFinal head `991d34b3f`. The second commit changes only `crates/post/tests/comp.rs` (the expected wear note `D2` becomes `D1`).\n\n- **winbuild** (Windows), log `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-4143-991d34b.log` (first line `991d34b3f51371920eed203054cf22a17c05597e`, trial merge with `origin/main` clean):\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: `cl suites: headless_bin` ok, `post build` ok, all 141 `post suites` steps ok (`comp`, `script_sinumerik`, `bore_cycle`, `ream_cycle`, `explain_remaining`, `wcs_flip_dialects`, `arc_planes`, `probe_dialects` included). The `app build (--no-run)` step stopped with `STALL` (45 min with no output while it linked the app test binaries on the 16 GB host). The app steps were thus not run on winbuild. This is a host stop, not a test failure.\n  - `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- **Mac**, quick gate on the first head `90b9c867b` (the same app code and app tests as the final head): 143 steps ok, 1 failed (`post suites: comp`, the expected `D2` note that the second commit corrects). The plan included the 840D suites and the shipped-example suites (`example_catalog*`, `first_part_programs`). Light lane 0 failed, strict clippy clean.\n- **Mac**, final head `991d34b3f`, by name: `sinumerik_safe_retract` (7), `program_comments` (4), `conformance` (7), `program_units` (7), `example_catalog` (43, 4 ignored), `example_catalog_adaptive` (1), `example_catalog_edge_work` (1): all pass.\n- P3: no heavy step.\n\nChangelog: Siemens 840D post: the tool call selects the first cutting edge (`T12 D1 M6`), and a machine file can state `tooling.d_number: \"tool-number\"` for D equal to T. Each G53 retract, the program end included, is now `G0 G53 Z.. D0`.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4143\nFixes #4144\n",
